**A live token update verified systemic propagation.** To test resilience against change, I modified a core UNDRR spacing variable from 30 pixels to 32 pixels in code and re-published the library. When I accepted the update in the pilot design file, the layout adjusted seamlessly. Every edited title, toggled preset, brand setting, and instance override survived intact; restoring the value returned the measured fields to their baseline.

**Interoperability validated the content architecture.** Because the components were generated from shared schemas, switching between UNDRR, PreventionWeb, and MCR2030 brand modes reshuffled colors, typography, and corner treatments instantly. The content structure remained unshakeable because the underlying shipping container had been standardized first.

## How do you balance automated generation with maintenance debt?

**Code generation brings its own maintenance obligations.** The reviewed pull request introduced roughly 77,000 lines of code, including around 33,000 lines of construction recipes, test suites, and developer audits. While the generator successfully proved that code-to-Figma pipelines can produce high-fidelity kits, maintaining an elaborate compiler pipeline alongside active product code represents substantial ongoing overhead.

**I chose a smaller ongoing commitment.** Instead of maintaining an all-in-one generator indefinitely, I decided to keep automated sync for lightweight tokens and styles, while reserving full structural component generation for major version overhauls or new component introductions. The [code split remains pending](https://github.com/unisdr/undrr-mangrove/pull/1319#issuecomment-5993683966), and manual edits need an ownership policy before a later rebuild.

**The bridge is a shared model across different working environments.** As with my work to [put analytics into editorial workflows](/work/2026/impact-story-undrr-analytics-overlay-mcp/), the real unlock was carrying existing domain rules into the environment where another discipline works. Lots of teams can draw a Figma kit or publish a Storybook. What made this work durable was grounding both in structured content and semantic models from day one, giving designers, developers, and AI agents a common vocabulary that scales.

